mingTypes"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Identifiable"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Identifiable\/ID-swift.associatedtype","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ID","preciseIdentifier":"s:s12IdentifiableP2IDQa"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Identifiable"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol to provide a stable notion of identity to a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"class or value type. For example, you could define a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"User"},{"type":"text","text":" type with an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property that is stable across your app and your app’s database storage."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"You could use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" property to identify a particular user even if other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"data fields change, such as the user’s name."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Identifiable"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves the duration and scope of the identity unspecified."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Identities can have any of the following characteristics:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Guaranteed always unique, like UUIDs."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Persistently unique per environment, like database record keys."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unique for the lifetime of a process, like global incrementing integers."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unique for the lifetime of an object, like object identifiers."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unique within the current collection, like collection indices."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It’s up to both the conformer and the receiver of the protocol to document"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the nature of the identity."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Conforming to the Identifiable Protocol","anchor":"Conforming-to-the-Identifiable-Protocol","type":"heading","level":1},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Identifiable"},{"type":"text","text":" provides a default implementation for class types (using"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ObjectIdentifier"},{"type":"text","text":"), which is only guaranteed to remain unique for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lifetime of an object. If an object has a stronger notion of identity, it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"may be appropriate to provide a custom implementation."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/identifiable"]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Identifiable\/ID-swift.associatedtype"],"title":"Specifying the Associated Type","anchor":"Specifying-the-Associated-Type"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Identifiable\/id-8t2ws"],"title":"Specifying the Identified Item","anchor":"Specifying-the-Identified-Item"}],"references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/Comparable":{"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Comparable"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitl